VAR npcEmotion = "Angry"

Ah, Mr. Wade Kim, welcome to the I.M.A. I'm Miss Maggie. #speaker:Maggie  
-> Start  

=== Start ===  
Hello, Miss Maggie. #speaker:Player  

You're our newest recruit. Big step, joining the I.M.A. We don’t take just anyone. You must have impressed someone. #speaker:Maggie  

* Thank you. I’ll do my best. #speaker:Player  
    -> Briefing  
* When do I start? #speaker:Player  
    No time to waste, huh? I like that. But first, we need to see if you’ve got what it takes. #speaker:Maggie  
    -> Continue  

=== Briefing ===  
Let’s get you up to speed. The Information Monitoring Agency (I.M.A.) —that’s us—deals with intelligence, deceptive narratives, and keeping the world from falling apart. It’s a big job, and you’re now part of it. #speaker:Maggie  

* Sounds important. What’s next? #speaker:Player  
    -> Continue  
* Deceptive narratives? Like propaganda? #speaker:Player  
    More than that. We track, analyze, and neutralize harmful information before it spreads. And sometimes... well, sometimes we handle things more directly. #speaker:Maggie  
    -> Continue  

=== Continue ===  
Alright, time to see what you’re made of. See that arcade machine over there? Go interact with it—you’ll get a code. Then, use the console beside it to input the code. That’ll send you straight to the training grounds.  

Pass the test, and you’re in. Fail… and, well, let’s not think about that. Prove yourself, Agent. #speaker:Maggie  
-> END